# DM26-0670

# infra/release-secrets-baseline.nuon
#
# Findings of the secret scan (noseyparker) that a person looked at and accepted, so the release gate does not stop for them again.
# A finding is named by its `finding_id`, which depends on the rule and the matched text, so it stays the same as the history grows.
# Write one with `nu infra/release.nu secrets accept ID --reason "why"`; it never holds the secret, only the id and the reason.
#
#   { id: "df3fbd860d...", reason: "an example value in the documentation" }
